[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Sicilian Defense: Alapin Variation"]
[Variation "Alapin Variation, Smith-Morra Declined"]
[ECO "B22"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "pin"]
[Themes "e5-wedge,tempo-gain,d4-pawn-centre"]
[Kind "main"]

1. e4 c5
2. c3 { Prepares d4, so White can build pawns on d4 and e4. If Black takes on d4, the c-pawn recaptures and White keeps a strong centre. [%cal Gc3d4] }
2... Nf6
3. e5 { Hits the knight at once. It has to move again, so Black has spent two moves on one piece while White has spent one. }
3... Nd5
4. d4 { Claims the centre now the knight has left. If Black takes on d4, White recaptures and keeps the pair of centre pawns. }
4... cxd4
(4... d6 5. Nf3 { Develops and keeps d4 guarded. If Black takes on e5, White can recapture with the knight. } 5... Nc6 6. Bc4 { Attacks the knight on d5, which must move again. } 6... Nb6 7. Bb3 { Keeps the bishop on the diagonal, aimed at f7, and out of range of the knight. } 7... dxe5 8. Nxe5 Nxe5 9. dxe5)
(4... e6 5. Nf3 cxd4 6. cxd4 d6 7. Bc4 Nb6 8. Bb3)
5. Nf3 { Develops and attacks the pawn on d4 a second time. White will win it back and keep the centre, so there is no need to hurry. }
5... Nc6
(5... e6 6. cxd4 d6 7. Bc4 Nb6 8. Bb3 { The bishop retreats with the diagonal to f7 still open, and Black's knight has no good square to attack it from. } 8... Nc6 9. O-O)
(5... d6 6. exd6 { Takes the pawn that advanced. Black has to recapture, and the pawn on d4 is still going to fall. } 6... e6 7. Nxd4 Bxd6 8. Be2)
6. cxd4 { Recaptures with the c-pawn, so White has pawns on d4 and e5 and Black has none in the centre. }
6... d6
7. Bc4 { Attacks the knight on d5. The d6 pawn blocks Black's queen, so nothing defends the knight and it has to move again. [%cal Gc4d5] }
7... Nb6
(7... dxe5 8. Nxe5)
(7... e6 8. O-O)
8. Bb5 { Gets the bishop away from the knight on b6 and pins the knight on c6, the piece guarding e5. Black cannot take on e5 safely. [%cal Gb5e8] }
8... dxe5
(8... Bd7 9. exd6)
(8... e6 9. exd6)
9. Nxe5 { Wins the pawn back. The knight on c6 is pinned to the king, so it cannot take on e5. }
9... Bd7
10. Nxd7 { Gets rid of the bishop that was about to unpin the knight. }
10... Qxd7
11. Nc3 { Brings out the last knight and covers d5 and e4, where Black's pieces want to land. }
11... e6
12. O-O { Plan: castle, put a rook on e1 and the bishop on f4 or g5, then use the extra space with d5 or Qd2. If Black leaves the book, finish development before opening the centre. } *
